The '''Pykes''' were a [[species]] of [[Sentience|sentient]] [[humanoid]]s native to the [[planet]] [[Oba Diah]]. The species had two distinct physiological groups. While both shared elongated heads, one group was characterized by their oversized [[Bone|craniums]] with undersized faces, while the other bore more humanoid proportions with [[Fish|piscine]] features. The [[Pyke Syndicate]] was [[the galaxy]]'s preeminent supplier of [[spice]], a narcotic substance [[Mining|mined]] by [[Slavery|slaves]] on the planet [[Kessel]].

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|Did you honestly think you'd get away with fooling a Pyke?|Marg Krim, to Trace and Rafa Martez|<ref name="Dangerous Debt">{{TCW|Dangerous Debt}}</ref>}}
[[File:Unlimited-LomPyke.png|thumb|left|300px|Examples of two forms of the Pyke species' body]]
A [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]], the Pykes were [[humanoid]], although most were slimmer and taller than most [[human]]s. They had two long, lanky [[Limb|legs]], and two arms that ended in three<ref name="Dark Disciple" />, four<ref name="Dealer in Truths" />, or five-fingered hands. Their heads were large and elongated, with a tapered [[Skeleton|skull]] and a proportionately undersized face, a feature which some other species found unsettling. Pykes had two narrow, almond-shaped [[eye]]s which could be [[Color|blue]], magenta,<ref name="Dark Disciple" /> purple,<ref name="Eminence" /> or black in color.<ref name="Chapter 2" /> Their heads rested upon elongated, sinuous necks. The species had two [[Gender|sexes]], male and female.<ref name="Dark Disciple" /> Pykes had yellow<ref name="Solo">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> or green blood.<ref name="In the Name of Honor">{{BOBF|Chapter 7: In the Name of Honor}}</ref>

Some Pykes had smaller craniums than others of the species,<ref name="Dealer in Truths">{{SWU|set=Shadows of the Galaxy|cardname=Lom Pyke|subtitle=Dealer in Truths|link=5632569775|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240612185415/https://swudb.com/card/shd/032/lom-pyke}}</ref> as well as short bloated necks, and five<ref name="Chapter 2" /> or four fingers.<ref name="Dealer in Truths" /> Whereas others of the species had a range skin tones including gray and green,<ref name="Eminence" /> these individuals might possessed teal skin with pink accents<ref name="Chapter 2" /> or a gray-green coloration like their tall brethren.<ref name="Dealer in Truths" /> Beneath the masks frequently worn by the species, the short-necked Pykes' faces resembled [[fish]].<ref name="Chapter 2" /> Another of this Pyke type, however, might have a larger head closer to that of their tall fellows.<ref name="Dealer in Truths" /> The atmosphere of the planet [[Kessel]] could provoke lethal allergic reactions in Pykes if they were exposed to it for too long, necessitating the wearing of special protective gear if they remained there long-term.<ref name="Alien Archive">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref>

==Society and culture==
{{Quote|I pay attention to the world around me, like the fact that the Pykes are gangsters!''"<br />"''Gangsters? What, like Pintu back on Coruscant?''"<br />"''No. ''Much'' worse. ''Galactically'' worse. They'll take your ''ship'', your ''life'', ''everything''!|Ahsoka Tano and Trace Martez, on the Pykes|<ref name="Deal No Deal">{{TCW|Deal No Deal}}</ref>}}
[[File:PykeSyndicateCapo-SWQ04.png|thumb|right|300px|High ranking Pykes in the Syndicate held the title of Capo.]]
Pykes hailed from [[Oba Diah]],<ref name="Pykes SWE" /> a terrestrial [[planet]] marked by [[obsidian]] cliffs. Visitors to Oba Diah viewed both the population and terrain as unwelcoming.<ref name="Dark Disciple" /> The Pyke [[homeworld]] served as the headquarters of the [[Pyke Syndicate]], a criminal organization which profited from distributing [[spice]], an illicit substance harvested by [[Slavery|slaves]] in the [[Spice mines of Kessel|spice mines]] of the planet [[Kessel]].<ref name="Pyke Syndicate DB" /> The Pykes on Kessel had to wear special breath masks and lead-lined clothing to protect themselves from the planet's harsh climate.<ref name="Alien Archive" /> To deliver spice to their customers, such as crime families on [[Coruscant]], the Pyke Syndicate relied on [[smuggler]]s and [[freighter]] [[captain]]s to complete the dangerous [[Kessel Run]].<ref name="Pyke Syndicate DB">{{Databank|pyke-syndicate|Pyke Syndicate}}</ref>

==History==
===Before the Clone Wars===
{{Quote|A powerful part of the spice cartel. Their criminal activities had allowed them to almost completely control the production of raw spice, used to create a powerful drug.|Former [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Finis Valorum]], on the Pyke Syndicate|<ref name="The Lost One">{{TCW|The Lost One}}</ref>}}
Before the [[Invasion of Naboo]], the Pyke Syndicate was set to enter clandestine negotiations with [[Sifo-Dyas]] to resolve an underground war. Unbeknownst to him, the Pykes had made an alliance with a man named [[Dooku|Tyranus]], who in fact was the former [[Jedi Master]] Dooku; Tyranus hired the Pykes to shoot down Sifo-Dyas' ship over the [[Oba Diah moon]], killing Sifo-Dyas. The Pykes subsequently locked up Sifo-Dyas' aide, [[Silman]], as insurance against Tyranus.<ref name="The Lost One" />

===Clone Wars===
{{Quote|Spice dealers connected to all the crime families on Coruscant.''"<br />"''The Pykes. They will be the next to join us.|[[Pre Vizsla]] and Maul|<ref name="Eminence" />}}
[[File:Pykes.png|thumb|left|275px|Pykes wearing their masks]]
During the [[Clone Wars]], the Pyke Syndicate, led by [[Lom Pyke]], joined the [[Shadow Collective]], a criminal alliance formed by [[Sith Lord]] [[Maul]]. The collective aimed to defeat the [[Galactic Republic]] and [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] by uniting [[the galaxy]]'s criminal underworld. Under Maul's guidance, the Pykes, the [[Black Sun]] cartel, and the [[Mandalorian]] extremists of [[Death Watch]] launched a [[Takeover of Mandalore|takeover]] of [[Mandalore]], which resulted in a planet-wide [[Mandalorian Civil War (19 BBY)|civil war]].<ref name="The Lawless">{{TCW|The Lawless}}</ref>

In [[19 BBY]], the Jedi traced Sifo-Dyas' lightsaber back to Oba Diah, where [[Anakin Skywalker]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] confront the crime syndicate. In exchange for Silman, the Pykes asked the Jedi to forget the act of treachery the former carried out against the latter. Tyranus arrived soon thereafter and engaged the Jedi and Pykes in battle, killing Lom.<ref name="The Lost One" />

[[Ahsoka Tano]] bore witness to the Pyke Syndicate's role in the spice trade when she accompanied the [[Martez family|Martez]] sisters to Kessel to pick up the spice and deliver it to Oba Diah.<ref name="Deal No Deal" /> Though they were captured by their current leader [[Marg Krim]],<ref name="Dangerous Debt" /> they eventually managed to escape, and Tano learned of the syndicate's alliance with Maul.<ref name="Together Again">{{TCW|Together Again}}</ref>

===Imperial Era===
{{Quote|Kill him and you'll be starting a war with Isa Durand. Call this a bad deal and walk away.''"<br />"''We do not accept bad deals.|Cid and a Pyke, as the latter threatens Roland Durand|<ref name="Infested">{{TBB|Infested}}</ref>}}
After the rise of the [[Galactic Empire]], the Pykes continued to expand their territory throughout the galaxy. At one point, they made a deal with the [[Devaronian]] [[Roland Durand]] of the [[Durand crime family]] in exchange for spice. However, the spice was stolen by [[Clone Force 99]] with the help of [[Ciddarin Scaleback|Cid]], leading the Pykes to threaten Durand's life. The spice was eventually returned to them and the Pykes punished Durand for his failure by cutting off one of his horns.<ref name="Infested" /> The Pyke who cut off Roland's horn would later be captured by Clone Force 99 and turned over to the Durand crime family in exchange for information. The Pyke was held prisoner by the family as punishment for the disgrace he brought upon them by cutting off Roland's horn.<ref>''[[Star Wars: The Bad Batch]]'' - "[[Paths Unknown]]"</ref>

The Pyke [[Quay Tolsite]] served as a capo in the Pyke Syndicate and overseer of a spice mine on Kessel until he was killed by [[Qi'ra]].<ref name="Solo" />

Later, a few members of the Pyke Syndicate attended the [[Auction for Han Solo|auction]] for [[Han Solo]] aboard the [[Vermillion (Crimson Dawn)|''Vermillion'']] on the planet [[Jekara]]. The auction was hosted by [[Lady]] [[Qi'ra]] and her recently returned crime syndicate [[Crimson Dawn]].<ref name="Doctor Aphra 12">[[Doctor Aphra (2020) 12|''Doctor Aphra'' (2020) 12]]</ref> The Pykes attempted to buy the smuggler, but were outbid by the [[Hutt Clan]].<ref name="War of the Bounty Hunters 2">[[War of the Bounty Hunters 2|''War of the Bounty Hunters'' 2]]</ref>

[[File:Gorak_Palas.png|thumb|right|200px|Gorak Palas was an underboss of the Pyke Syndicate who commanded the syndicate's operation in Toshara.]]
In [[3 ABY]], the Pyke Syndicate possessed great power on the [[moon]] [[Toshara]], with its operation on the world, which involved an agreement with the Empire, being commanded by [[Gorak Palas]]. Although almost the entire moon was Pyke territory, the syndicate's hold on Toshara was threatened by other crime syndicates, such as the Hutt Clan and [[Crimson Dawn]].<ref name="Outlaws">''[[Star Wars Outlaws]]''</ref>

===Post-Empire===
{{Quote|Let me tell you something, Pykes do not mess around. Ever since they've been moving spice through the system, everything's gone to hell.|[[Peli Motto]], to [[Din Djarin]]|<ref name="Chapter 5">{{BOBF|Chapter 5: Return of the Mandalorian}}</ref>}}
In [[5 ABY]],<ref name="BOBF 2 flashback date">{{InsiderCite|225|A Certain Point of View}} states that flashback events of "[[Chapter 2: The Tribes of Tatooine]]" took place five [[Standard year|years]] after the events of [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'' Episode IV ''A New Hope'']], corresponding to [[5 ABY]] according to ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''.</ref> a [[Tatooine repulsor train|train]] of Pykes regularly terrorized a [[Unidentified Tusken Raider tribe|Tusken tribe]] that [[Boba Fett]] resided in, before Fett and several of the [[Tusken Raider|Tuskens]] captured the Pykes on the train and made them walk to [[Anchorhead]] and fly off [[Tatooine]].<ref name="Chapter 2" /> Circa 5 ABY,<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> sometime after that incident, Fett went to the Pykes' headquarters on Tatooine and spoke to the [[Pyke Boss|leader]] of the Pykes in the area. Fett asked the Pyke boss to pay protection [[Currency|money]] to the Tusken tribe as promised. The Pyke boss said that he could not pay protection money to two groups, according to his superiors on Oba Diah, and informed Fett that the [[Kintan Striders Gang|Kintan Striders]] were already being paid protection money.<ref name="Chapter 3">{{BOBF|Chapter 3: The Streets of Mos Espa}}</ref>

By 9 ABY,<ref name="BOBF date">{{BoBFDate}}</ref> Jabba's former holdings on Tatooine had been promised to the Pykes by [[mayor]] [[Mok Shaiz]]. Then, a number of Pykes arrived on Tatooine from a [[Unidentified passenger starliner|starliner]].<ref name="Chapter 3" /> They continued to establish themselves as a dominating presence on the planet, including in the cities of [[Mos Espa]] and [[Mos Eisley]]. [[Law enforcement agency|Law enforcement]] refused to interfere with them.<ref name="Chapter 5" />

Later, [[marshal]] [[Cobb Vanth]] interrupted a Pykes spice trade in [[Freetown]] territory, and told the Pykes that he wouldn't tolerate the spice trade in the town. The Pykes tried to kill him due to his meddling, but Vanth drew his blaster faster and killed all but one who backed out of the fight. Vanth told him to go back and inform the syndicate of his ban, but not without taking the spice and throwing it away. To solve the problem, the Pyke Syndicate sent bounty hunter [[Cad Bane]]. When Bane was unable to convince Vanth to change his mind, the two had a [[Showdown in Freetown|duel]] that ended with Bane injuring Vanth and killing [[Scott]], the marshal's [[deputy]]. Later, they [[Destruction of Garsa Fwip's Sanctuary|bombed]] the [[Garsa Fwip's Sanctuary|Sanctuary]], killing many who were inside.<ref name="From the Desert">{{BOBF|Chapter 6: From the Desert Comes a Stranger}}</ref> After a [[Battle of Mos Espa|battle]] that took place in the streets of Mos Espa, the Pykes decided to leave the world due to the numerous losses caused by the battle, although [[Master Assassin]] [[Fennec Shand]] [[Assassination of the Pyke Syndicate leaders|assassinated]] the Pyke leaders on Tatooine before they could leave.<ref name="In the Name of Honor" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Pyke-concept.jpg|thumb|right|237x237px|Pyke concept art by [[Colin Fix]]]]
The Pykes were developed by [[George Lucas]] for the animated television series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''.<ref name="Shadows of the Sith">{{SW|url=video/shadows-of-the-sith|series=Clone Wars Download|text=Shadows of the Sith}}</ref> The species debuted in the [[The Clone Wars: Season Five|season five]] episode "[[Eminence (episode)|Eminence]]," which first aired in [[2013]].<ref name="Eminence" /> The design that became the Pykes originated in an April 2007 sketch of a Jedi character by [[David Hobbins]], which was then selected by Lucas. In mid-2009, [[Douglas Wheatley]] refined their looks, and they were planned for inclusion in the canceled game ''[[Star Wars: 1313]]''.<ref name="Art of Solo">''[[The Art of Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> The [[2018]] film ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'' marked the live-action debut for the species,<ref name="Solo" /> although they would not appear without a mask until ''[[Star Wars: The Book of Boba Fett]]''. This live action design<ref name="Chapter 2" /> differs from the animated Pyke design first featured in ''The Clone Wars''.<ref name="Eminence" /> Instead of it simply being a case of a species appearing differently between mediums, a ''[[Star Wars: Unlimited]]'' card drawn by [[Amad Mir]] would confirm both designs co-existed in universe.<ref name="Dealer in Truths" />

